 as a housekeeping or a new target gene?</article-title><source>BMC Cancer</source><year>2006</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>49</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16515701</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2407-6-49</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Selvey</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>EW</given-names></name><name><surname>Matthaei</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Lea</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Irving</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Beta-actin &#x02013; an unsuitable internal control for RT-PCR</article-title><source>Mol Cell Probes</source><year>2001</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>311</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11735303</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/mcpr.2001.0376</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arukwe</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Toxicological housekeeping genes: do they really keep the house?</article-title><source>Environ Sci Technol</source><year>2006</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>7944</fpage><lpage>7949</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17256553</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/es0615223</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tricarico</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinzani</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bianchi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Paglierani</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Distante</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><su